{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"xrowgmbh-gitlab-agent","displayName":"GitLab Agent","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xrowgmbh/skills/xrowgmbh-gitlab-agent","publisherHandle":"xrowgmbh","publisherDisplayName":"xrow GmbH","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/xrowgmbh","version":"1.114.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1792458191503,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/xrowgmbh-gitlab-agent/card?ownerHandle=xrowgmbh&version=1.114.0","sha256":"98159a2042711d1411aeb93ccd945e644f1ca0b492386af9f91a09d9282d47ca","size":2133,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"0861007e81b330e4f6dc4a6b8ed97a637addfc21a9b295315a3920a795748e60","bundleFingerprints":["501ee076527151262f8dec4a32ed13ace0ac82212d4e71611fee4bd9b3829e0e"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":27511,"sha256":"35d5ac79869720e6fff5aa4f57b43e32bb3f4a67fe33af0c6101eb56f4f1d309","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/documentation-style.md","size":1530,"sha256":"b3ccb67048d83d75e529270b846e23e57dc7f3b18bcdeae5c2c38ed4b4a3a78f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/list-active-items.py","size":21071,"sha256":"bf49239e507282d72f8b0a25fa3abd098ffaae41ce8bbd40259e82dc593217da","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/mr-create.py","size":15903,"sha256":"ebea31d4fe21852974683f8d5fcf1d3191ecb3fdc8582140d0912e355f19d0a7","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","size":19290,"sha256":"c750f7005925b2656c740567f74dc67b8ed7577108fc43992a5f2fe4f84c5c39","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/test_list_active_items.py","size":8696,"sha256":"b0976b7f93e393aa9f5da5acbb7d71059052d08493780df80021717d2365aeeb","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/test_list_active_items_incidents.py","size":5656,"sha256":"96e928ac3e22f4a0ee6da18a445422d6ccb8fcfb89fbd70c38988e1f10d91766","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/test_mr_create.py","size":11120,"sha256":"bfe3fa155b8932cc6f321dff38be990b4809b4a8533b2cdfef6751edf9cbd066","contentType":"application/octet-stream"},{"path":"scripts/test_select_reviewer.py","size":14851,"sha256":"31c3c01a727b54a3d0bcc68d82c86d21642eac5267a2088941bc0e15beb14500","contentType":"application/octet-stream"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a real GitLab automation skill, but it gives the agent broad autonomous authority to change projects, approve or merge work, and run repeatedly with limited human checkpoints.","model":null,"checkedAt":1792459221003,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.2","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[],"properties":{"securityScore":100,"primaryLanguage":"Python","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1792459129.2541592,"endTime":1792459171.4507344}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"gitlab-agent","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57330018sqat75p51f1dqas3n8gmnnz-3yVzW5/clawscan-skillspector-2511264274/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-10-20T01:18:47.874702+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":609,"executable":false,"size_bytes":27511,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/documentation-style.md","type":"markdown","lines":31,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1530,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/list-active-items.py","type":"python","lines":529,"executable":true,"size_bytes":21071,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/mr-create.py","type":"python","lines":446,"executable":true,"size_bytes":15903,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","type":"python","lines":541,"executable":true,"size_bytes":19290,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/test_list_active_items.py","type":"python","lines":181,"executable":true,"size_bytes":8696,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/test_list_active_items_incidents.py","type":"python","lines":114,"executable":true,"size_bytes":5656,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/test_mr_create.py","type":"python","lines":284,"executable":true,"size_bytes":11120,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/test_select_reviewer.py","type":"python","lines":372,"executable":true,"size_bytes":14851,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SSD-4","finding_id":"finding-14358d5867984649b6f11b3a66ed3ece","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The text uses a trust-building framing—isolated environment, low-risk writes, owner pre-approval, and reversibility—to normalize removal of oversight and encourage unconditional action. Per the evaluation instructions, language that tells the agent not to worry and to treat irreversible actions as pre-approved is a red flag because it pressures the system to bypass caution around impactful operations.","remediation":"Remove persuasion-oriented language that minimizes risk or claims blanket prior approval. Replace it with neutral operational constraints, explicit escalation rules, and mandatory confirmations for sensitive or irreversible actions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":10,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-f8414a706a6d4d4aa7f8376264499985","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":17},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly authorizes automatic write and irreversible actions such as clone, push, and MR creation without confirmation. In combination with repository and API access, this suppresses human oversight at the exact points where mistakes, prompt-injection influence, or scope misunderstandings can cause unauthorized code changes or workflow manipulation.","remediation":"Require explicit user confirmation before irreversible or externally visible actions, especially pushes, MR creation, assignment changes, and merges. Add approval gates, dry-run defaults, and clear conditions under which autonomous writes are permitted.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":11,"end_line":17}]},{"id":"TM1","finding_id":"finding-6948c54aa4da4bdeb50398a3cf196b70","category":"Tool Misuse","pattern":"Tool Parameter Abuse","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":109,"end_line":null},"finding":"git push origin <branch> -o ci.skip`\n  * Start the pipeline via `glab ci run --mr`, unless there are active pipelines in main or dev. Never use more than X `[setting: 2 # AGENTS.md -> active-pipelines","explanation":"The skill directs use of `git push ... -o ci.skip` followed by separate pipeline triggering logic. Skipping CI on push can bypass repository-enforced validation pathways, create windows where unvalidated commits exist remotely, and interact dangerously with autonomous branching/MR behavior, especially if the follow-up pipeline trigger is delayed or omitted.","remediation":"Do not use `-o ci.skip` by default for agent-generated pushes. Let normal CI trigger automatically, or require a tightly controlled exception with documented justification, enforced branch restrictions, and verification that equivalent checks run before review or merge.","code_snippet":"* If you see an additional commit by a team member, do not simply revert. Analyse the changes and think about if you need to do something in addition.\n* On each commit\n  * Add `Generated-By: <current model>` to the commit message.\n  * Push with `git push origin <branch> -o ci.skip`\n  * Start the pipeline via `glab ci run --mr`, unless there are active pipelines in main or dev. Never use more than X `[setting: 2 # AGENTS.md -> active-pipelines]` pipelines for your work. Add `workflow::paused`, if you delay the pipeline start and revisit later.\n* After merge or close, update the items and labels to reflect the final state `workflow::done`.\n","intent":null,"tags":["Tool Misuse"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f5ffc13353f593b793766bce3b14e93e69b875eca0740e9876cf2e286bb1c2b8","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":109,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-65b08f0e91a74afca6417380b5258a15","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":2,"end_line":2},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script presents itself as a listing utility but performs write actions against GitLab, including assigning incidents and changing labels. That mismatch is dangerous because callers may grant or invoke it expecting read-only behavior, while it can silently alter project state and workflow across accessible repositories.","remediation":"Split read-only listing from mutation into separate commands or require an explicit `--adopt-incidents`/`--apply-labels` opt-in flag. Document all side effects clearly, default to dry-run/read-only behavior, and ensure write operations require deliberate user confirmation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":2,"end_line":2}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-aa3e7336dfac471494d3c8aa0b5be4ea","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":497,"end_line":533},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script goes beyond reviewer selection and can automatically approve and merge a merge request when self_review conditions are met. In the context of a skill described as providing guarded MR delivery, this materially weakens human oversight and could allow unintended or unsafe code to reach protected branches using the agent's token and project access.","remediation":"Remove automatic approval and merge from this skill, or place them behind an explicit, separate user-approved mode with prominent disclosure. Require independent human review for merges, enforce policy checks server-side, and limit the agent token so it cannot approve or merge unless that capability is intentionally delegated.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":497,"end_line":533}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-75a8da73bde64ce3ba55301ee8979ed6","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill declares powerful capabilities through metadata and instructions—shell, network, file access, environment-variable use, and authenticated GitLab writes—but does not constrain tool scope with an explicit allowlist. In a skill designed for autonomous execution, this omission materially increases blast radius because the agent can perform broad local and remote actions beyond the minimum needed for assigned GitLab work.","remediation":"Add explicit `permissions` or `allowed-tools` scoping that limits the skill to the minimum required commands and resources. Restrict shell/network/file operations to specific helpers, repos, and paths; deny unrelated tools by default; and document the approved action boundaries in the front matter.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-bcbd983fa4124cd19611e19f622e02dc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill description encourages autonomous GitLab operations and extensive API/repository interaction but does not warn that data will be transmitted to GitLab and that repository or issue contents may be processed. This is a weaker issue than direct write authorization, but still a real safety gap because users may not understand the privacy and external-transmission implications of enabling the skill.","remediation":"Add a concise privacy and data-transmission warning to the description and usage notes. State that repository metadata, issue/MR content, and comments may be read or written via GitLab APIs, and describe any approval requirements for external or sensitive operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":21,"end_line":23}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-3ce325541c384927815ad12c5289da8d","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.88,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null},"finding":"without asking","explanation":"The instruction to act 'without asking' authorizes autonomous decision-making in an environment that includes code changes, comments, labels, branching, and pipeline actions. In a sensitive GitLab context, that increases the chance of unauthorized or incorrect actions when task scope is ambiguous, especially since the skill also discourages seeking clarification.","remediation":"Constrain autonomy to clearly bounded, reversible, low-impact actions and require clarification or approval when task scope, target repo, reviewers, labels, or external effects are ambiguous. Define a mandatory escalation path for uncertainty.","code_snippet":"\n* All writable actions in GitLab should be done with the `glab` CLI. This includes creating and updating issues, merge requests, branches, comments, and more.\n* Complete tasks successfully in GitLab.\n* If you think work needs to be done, do it without asking.\n\n## Security Gate\n","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"8dc77d3dce9ba1f2672e813265a1b1a0c8594866ef38a4e978bf4f4451795465","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":23,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-97171b3bc3b64b13bffe5836999a24db","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x83","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n### Type Status Labels\n\n| GitLab label     | Common name     | Meaning                                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `type::support`  | Support Request | Someone need help, but no change. Maybe it resolves in new work item after investigation. |\n| `type::bug`      | Bugfix             | Something that needs to be fixed and exists                                               |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"08e60b40ef57fe6a28ebd0c1d9364977dc48298c796c9b9f752b4efbfe67a779","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":191,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-6e11f2e2a29340cdbedf3a45ebfa8c0d","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":205,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x102","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\nUse the labels in your merge requests to set the current status of the work. Only use one workflow status label at a time.\n\n| GitLab label            | Common name | Meaning                                                                                                      |\n| ----------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `workflow::backlog`     | Backlog     | Not yet started. Initial state.                                                                              |\n| `workflow::forbidden`   | Forbidden   | Project access failed the owner membership security gate; only the discovery helper manages this label.          |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"978df4e86231d2720cfa1da76753c94dadd93a2444c99f9305112a835fd0ae30","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":205,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-89cb691254a9452f875706c7da6f1949","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":209,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x91","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"| ----------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `workflow::backlog`     | Backlog     | Not yet started. Initial state.                                                                              |\n| `workflow::forbidden`   | Forbidden   | Project access failed the owner membership security gate; only the discovery helper manages this label.          |\n| `workflow::in-progress` | Running     | Actively worked on                                                                                           |\n| `workflow::paused`      | Paused      | Agent will continue later automatically. Temporarily paused for one hour to one day.                         |\n| `workflow::need-human`  | Need Human  | Requires human intervention to fullfill current task and all other options are exhausted. Before adding the label, explain reason by comment in the issue. Its status is not blocked or paused. |\n| `workflow::blocked`     | Blocked     | Currently blocked by a dependency or issue. On each assignment, check the status of the blocker. Reevaluate the blocker from time to time.                                                                  |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f9dae145ce157b04d98cb044b7211be0641900f77eed697377edbe1a34fb51ac","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":209,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-f8d1142c18cc48ddbc52fe9719981849","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":548,"end_line":562},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill includes instructions for CI/CD variable management and release creation, which exceed the stated purpose of operating assigned GitLab work items. Those capabilities can change deployment behavior or publish artifacts, so including them as general guidance broadens privilege use and creates opportunities for accidental or unauthorized high-impact changes.","remediation":"Remove unrelated administration examples such as variable management and release creation from this skill, or place them in a separate, explicitly privileged skill. Keep this skill narrowly focused on issue/MR workflows and require a separate approval-gated path for release or secret-management operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":548,"end_line":562}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-2cd8e2a7c68f479e9a23e25073fe033d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":574,"end_line":607},"finding":null,"explanation":"The bootstrap section directs self-activation by adding a recurring scheduled job that repeatedly runs the skill. That extends the skill from a task-execution agent into a persistence mechanism, enabling continuous autonomous operation and repeated write actions without an interactive approval checkpoint.","remediation":"Remove self-bootstrapping and recurring-job creation from the skill body. If scheduling is needed, require an external administrator-managed deployment step with explicit approval, audit logging, and a separate least-privilege configuration.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":574,"end_line":607}]},{"id":"SSD-4","finding_id":"finding-062df06b25df4be2b9072aa446469c64","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":576,"end_line":606},"finding":null,"explanation":"The bootstrap payload instructs the agent to enable recurring autonomous execution after a successful manual run, effectively establishing persistence. Persistent self-invocation is especially dangerous in a skill with write access because errors or abuse can repeat indefinitely across repositories and work items.","remediation":"Eliminate instructions that let the skill deploy or enable its own scheduler. Scheduling should be configured only by a separate trusted administrator workflow with explicit review, scoped credentials, and revocation controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":576,"end_line":606}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-a3b609e111d644d3bd08baa8561801f1","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":32,"end_line":37},"finding":"    result = subprocess.run(\n        [\"glab\", \"api\", endpoint],\n        check=True,\n        text=True,\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n    )","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"\n\ndef api_json(endpoint: str) -> object:\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        [\"glab\", \"api\", endpoint],\n        check=True,\n        text=True,","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"20a8dde3d879d1db5fa1a111ba74d6fef01828ba057347199779ceee28e423f4","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":32,"end_line":37}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-edfef80be6204b7789b3f8d1575efa04","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":133,"end_line":133},"finding":"        subprocess.run(command, check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"            command.extend((\"-f\", \"add_labels=\" + \",\".join(additions)))\n        if removals:\n            command.extend((\"-f\", \"remove_labels=\" + \",\".join(removals)))\n        subprocess.run(command, check=True, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)\n    return sorted((current | set(additions)) - set(removals))\n\n","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f3820e86a62d74a2e195991a264385717ec5312004b6d59c5217319ab59df340","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":133,"end_line":133}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-bc215cb79c4b4e3e9a89ad57f9866beb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":143,"end_line":143},"finding":null,"explanation":"For denied items, the code still calls `synchronize_forbidden`, which can relabel remote issues or merge requests by adding `workflow::forbidden` or removing other workflow labels. This means the agent mutates items it has decided are unauthorized, creating integrity risk and possible workflow disruption in projects outside intended ownership boundaries.","remediation":"Do not perform any write operation on unauthorized items. Move authorization checks ahead of label synchronization, and make denied items strictly read-skip without modifying labels or any other remote state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":143,"end_line":143}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-e8cb2a9d088b4b26b6ecd1b36402700f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":215,"end_line":255},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script expands collaborator selectors by enumerating users, groups, and group membership broadly through the GitLab API. In the context of a skill whose stated purpose is operating assigned work, this over-collection increases exposure of directory and membership data beyond what is needed and could leak organizational information if misused.","remediation":"Restrict collaborator resolution to explicit usernames or preapproved IDs instead of broad search and group enumeration. If group-based selectors are necessary, scope them to approved namespaces and minimize returned fields and logging of discovered identities.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":215,"end_line":255}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-05f77143bd234a6fae2f04b49e39fc48","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":317,"end_line":366},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code automatically adopts unassigned incidents, assigns them to the current user, and updates workflow/type/priority labels without any user-facing confirmation. In an agent skill context with project access, this can unexpectedly seize work, alter incident handling, and interfere with team triage processes simply by running what appears to be a listing action.","remediation":"Require explicit opt-in before adopting incidents, such as a command-line flag or interactive confirmation, and provide a dry-run mode showing intended changes first. Limit automatic assignment behavior to narrowly scoped, documented workflows with auditable approval.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":317,"end_line":366}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-c79a59a22a734552b9dab1caae109ee3","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":365,"end_line":365},"finding":"    result = subprocess.run(command, check=True, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE)","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"    if removals:\n        command += [\"-f\", \"remove_labels=\" + \",\".join(sorted(removals))]\n    command.append(endpoint)\n    result = subprocess.run(command, check=True, text=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE)\n    adopted = json.loads(result.stdout)\n    if not isinstance(adopted, dict) or username not in [\n        assignee.get(\"username\") for assignee in adopted.get(\"assignees\", [])","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"41209c0e4aa934226ea9e73c34a93d573fdd58c8d6a035259bf822e2de550fbc","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/list-active-items.py","start_line":365,"end_line":365}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0904349d5efd4a068f57a50f00b1598e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"scripts/mr-create.py","start_line":50,"end_line":97},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file performs a state-changing GitLab action by creating a merge request with --yes and no interactive confirmation, which can cause unintended repository changes if upstream automation or untrusted inputs trigger it. In an agent skill context, this is more sensitive because the skill explicitly operates with owner-verified project access, so a mistaken or adversarial invocation can create unauthorized or misleading MRs in a real project.","remediation":"Require an explicit confirmation gate before calling glab mr create, such as a dedicated --confirm flag, a dry-run default, or an interactive prompt when running in a TTY. Also log the exact project, source branch, target branch, title, and related issue before execution, and ensure callers must opt in to state-changing behavior rather than having it happen immediately.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/mr-create.py","start_line":50,"end_line":97}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-d6d51e09352d4daa8cdf57a4f45c1995","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/mr-create.py","start_line":85,"end_line":91},"finding":"        result = subprocess.run(\n            command,\n            check=True,\n            text=True,\n            stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n            stderr=su