,"pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":28,"end_line":34},"finding":"    result = subprocess.run(\n        [\"glab\", \"api\", endpoint],\n        check=True,\n        text=True,\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n    )","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"\n\ndef api_text(endpoint: str) -> str:\n    result = subprocess.run(\n        [\"glab\", \"api\", endpoint],\n        check=True,\n        text=True,","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"52539d188bcc65082aa40722ce4c43a2e784ebe555ad6a11c9420a2af40873f9","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":28,"end_line":34}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-6e94ac95dde541b7ae3949c602b2fbeb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":133,"end_line":174},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill's stated purpose is operating assigned GitLab work with owner-verified project access, but this code also reads a local configuration file whose path may be supplied by an environment variable. Accessing local host configuration is not an obvious requirement of GitLab reviewer selection itself, and introduces an extra capability outside the core remote-project workflow.","remediation":"Document local configuration access explicitly in the skill scope, or move reviewer-ignore settings into GitLab-resident configuration that matches the skill's declared purpose and access model.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":133,"end_line":174}]},{"id":"EA2","finding_id":"finding-645a19bd4a024a8da0583894a08c4a20","category":"Excessive Agency","pattern":"Autonomous Decision Making","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.75,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":178,"end_line":null},"finding":"no approval","explanation":"Skill enables autonomous high-impact decisions without human-in-the-loop verification. Critical operations (destructive commands, financial transactions, data deletion) should require explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add human-in-the-loop confirmation for destructive, irreversible, or high-impact operations. Never auto-execute commands that modify files, send data, or alter system state.","code_snippet":"\n\ndef optional_approval(endpoint: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Require both MR approval APIs to prove that no approval rule is required.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        approvals = json.loads(api_text(f\"{endpoint}/approvals\"))\n        state = json.loads(api_text(f\"{endpoint}/approval_state\"))","intent":null,"tags":["Excessive Agency","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"02114119728c4c9031d411902239e1c4b76f46eb7c1932c9ae63fcbe2fd1030c","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":178,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-424bd17231a844d6be6cbb20748e545a","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":428,"end_line":533},"finding":null,"explanation":"When run with --apply, the script can assign reviewers, approve, and merge without any interactive confirmation or strong user-facing disclosure at the point of action. In an autonomous agent setting, silent state-changing behavior increases the chance of surprising repository modifications and reduces operator ability to catch unsafe or unintended actions before they happen.","remediation":"Add explicit pre-action disclosure and confirmation for reviewer changes, approvals, and merges, especially for self-merge paths. Separate dry-run from apply modes more visibly, log intended side effects before execution, and require an affirmative flag dedicated to approval/merge actions instead of coupling them to reviewer application.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":428,"end_line":533}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-975d2850a8b84dbba13d9ec7958505a8","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":475,"end_line":492},"finding":"            subprocess.run(\n                [\n                    \"glab\",\n                    \"api\",\n                    \"-X\",\n                    \"PUT\",\n                    endpoint,\n                ","explanation":"subprocess module calls execute external commands. Without careful input validation, this enables command injection.","remediation":"Use subprocess.run() with shell=False and an explicit argument list. Validate all inputs and avoid passing user-controlled data to commands.","code_snippet":"            }\n        )\n        try:\n            subprocess.run(\n                [\n                    \"glab\",\n                    \"api\",","intent":null,"tags":["Dangerous Code Execution","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"fa70c377d01c8972b6cfaadb1fb1d0b82792e277f4d53ef4951f795c69668925","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":475,"end_line":492}]},{"id":"AST4","finding_id":"finding-907ab1c6f12044478ab418921fc50b6c","category":"Dangerous Code Execution","pattern":"subprocess module call","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"scripts/select-reviewer.py","start_line":499,"end_line":508},"finding":"                subproces