sion tests for deterministic reviewer selection, but several tests exercise materially broader behavior: applying reviewer changes, self-approval, and automatic merge flows. Those behaviors go beyond reviewer selection and touch MR state transitions, which is a meaningful expansion of intent relative to the documented purpose.","remediation":"Update the file/module documentation to reflect that the test suite also covers reviewer application, approval, and merge behaviors, or split merge-related tests into a separately documented test module.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/test_select_reviewer.py","start_line":2,"end_line":317}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-d813c435b12243c4a47a90d3e1be2fcb","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"scripts/test_select_reviewer.py","start_line":2,"end_line":317},"finding":null,"explanation":"The docstring states the file is for deterministic reviewer selection regression tests, but the implemented tests explicitly verify approval and merge command execution, including '/approve' and '/merge' calls. This is an active contradiction in stated intent versus exercised behavior, not merely an omitted implementation detail.","remediation":"Revise the docstring to describe the full scope of the suite, including self-review approval and merge-path regression coverage, or move those tests into a module whose documentation matches that behavior.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/test_select_reviewer.py","start_line":2,"end_line":317}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":true,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"mcp_tool_poisoning","request_kind":"structured_outp